{
  "slug": "big-egg-white-potato-breakfast-plate",
  "name": "Big egg white and potato breakfast plate",
  "description": "A large plate for a big morning: coarsely grated russet potato crisped with onion and mushrooms, topped with a soft egg white scramble enriched with a few whole eggs and finished with wilted spinach.",
  "iconKey": "crosshair",
  "instructions": [
    "Coarsely grate the potato, press it dry in a clean towel and spread it into a wide skillet with half the olive oil over medium-high heat.",
    "Scatter the onion and the mushrooms over the top, season with half the salt and all of the black pepper, and cook for 8 minutes, turning once, until the edges crisp.",
    "Meanwhile beat the egg white with the egg and the remaining salt, then scramble them in a second skillet with the rest of the olive oil over medium heat until only just set, about 4 minutes.",
    "Fold the spinach through the scramble until it wilts, then divide the hash and the scramble between two plates."
  ],
